# Trust bundle for gitlab.ss-wlabid.net, used as ca_path by the uri tasks.
#
# INCOMPLETE - what is below is the SERVER (leaf) certificate, not a CA. On its
# own it does not verify anything: OpenSSL will not accept a non-self-signed
# leaf as a trust anchor, so verification still fails with
# "error 20: unable to get local issuer certificate" - the very error this file
# is meant to fix. It also expires 2026-10-07 and will be reissued, whereas the
# CA below it lasts for years.
#
# To finish this file, append the issuing CA chain. The leaf's AIA extension
# says where it lives (HashiCorp Vault):
#
#   curl -s https://vault.stalsp-wlabid.net:8200/v1/pki_int/ca_chain \
#     >> roles/offboarding_gitlab/files/gitlab-ca-bundle.crt
#
# Then check it before committing - this must print "OK":
#
#   openssl verify -CAfile roles/offboarding_gitlab/files/gitlab-ca-bundle.crt \
#     ~/Downloads/gitlab.ss-wlabid.net.crt
#
# Once the chain is in, the leaf below is redundant and can be dropped.

